# spa-new coding style

Write code the same way it is written in `arcwood-ecommerce`: short, plain, no ceremony.
A mid-level dev should read any file top to bottom without jumping around.

## Architecture

1. **Route / page** — fetch data, unwrap with `getResponseData`, pass props down.
2. **Feature `helpers.ts`** — map API shapes into simple view data.
3. **Components** — render props only. No fetch. No API mapping.

## Pages (`src/app/[locale]/**/page.tsx`)

- `export const revalidate = 60;` at the top when the page hits the API.
- Props type above the component: `type AboutPageProps = { params: Promise<{ locale: string }> };`
  and reuse it in `generateMetadata`. No inline `{ params }: { params: Promise<...> }`.
- Fetch then unwrap on two lines:
  ```ts
  const res = await fetchAboutData(locale);
  const about = getResponseData<AboutData>(res);
  ```
  Not `getResponseData(await fetchX())` nested in one line.
- Tiny page-only helpers (like `parsePage`) live in the page file, not in `lib`.

## Async in server components

- One `await` per line: `const t = await getTranslations("x"); const locale = await getLocale();`
- `Promise.all` only for real parallel **API requests**, never for `getTranslations` / `getLocale`.
- Locale flag is always `const isAr = locale === "ar";` (not `isRtl`).

## API layer (`src/api`)

- Shared request logic lives in `client.ts` (`apiGet` / `apiPost`).
- Each `*Service.ts` is one path per function. No copy-pasted try/catch.

## Helpers & content

- Use `asArray` / `getResponseData` from `src/lib/content.ts`.
- Keep feature helpers next to the feature (`WhoWeAre/helpers.ts`, `Projects/helpers.ts`, …).
- One helper = one job. Name it after what it returns (`mapPartners`, `getWhatWeDoItems`).

## Components

- `"use client"` is always line 1. Imports after it. Nothing above it.
- Props type is `type XProps = { ... }` right above the component.
- Derive plain consts at the top, then a single `return`.
- Early return when there is nothing to show.
- No unused props renamed with `_`. Remove them from the type and from callers.

## Comments

- Use `// one short line` only. No `/** JSDoc */` blocks.
- Comment the *why* when it is not obvious. Do not describe what the code already says.

## Before you finish

- `npm run format` then `npm run lint` then `npx tsc --noEmit`. All three must be clean.
- No unused imports, props, or variables. Delete them, do not rename with `_`.
- No `setState` directly inside `useEffect`. Reset-on-prop-change → `key` remount or adjust state during render. Browser values (theme, size) → `useSyncExternalStore`.
- Icons from API strings go through `<DynamicIcon name="..." />`, never `const Icon = getIcon(...)` in render.

## Writing style

- Readable > clever. Explicit > abstract.
- Small files > giant "utils" dumps. Do not add layers "just in case".
- Match existing naming in the folder before inventing new patterns.
- Never change Tailwind classes / design while restyling code.
